Words denoting relatives, groups and places usually give negative values;
some plural abstractions give positive ones. WordNet supplies semantic
classes (using any listed sense, without disambiguation).
Scope stops at function words or punctuation and lasts at most five tokens.
A nested possessive ending also gives a negative response. Plurality uses
an s-ending heuristic plus a few irregular plurals.
This is a coarse English approximation, not a token-by-token lookup.
