The largest negative estimates are for short, consonant-ending pieces
which extend a word to five through seven letters. Uncommon English word
prefixes and vowel-initial pieces strengthen that estimate. Other pieces
have small offsets. Romanization lets the same spelling rules apply across
scripts; this is an approximation, not a dictionary of token identities.
